#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/algorithms/segment-intersection/bo/help/HelpContent.tsx:48
msgid "help.VerticalRules.2"
msgstr "A vertical segment in the active list represents an unfinished upward processing frontier. Its rank in the drawing is placed at the current processing height, not at a unique intersection with the sweep line. When it meets a crossing segment, processing first retains the previous order and records the intersection. Once complete, the vertical segment is placed above that crossing segment and checks new neighbors higher up. The whole vertical segment is complete only after removal at its upper endpoint."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/algorithms/segment-intersection/bo/help/HelpContent.tsx:47
msgid "help.VerticalRules.1"
msgstr "A vertical segment overlaps the sweep line along an interval, so a single ordinary line intersection cannot represent it. The x-then-y convention still applies: insert it at its lower endpoint, process crossings and contacts at successive heights, then record closed-segment contacts at its upper endpoint before removing it."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/algorithms/segment-intersection/bo/help/HelpContent.tsx:37
msgid "help.SamePointRules.2"
msgstr "A zero-length input has coincident start and end points, so it belongs to both groups. It never enters the continuing active order and has no corresponding insertion or removal action. Its intersections with segments or other points at the same location are recorded pair by pair; coincident coordinates do not merge input identities. The active order of a point-only set is always empty, but real events and pair results still exist."

