msgstr "Both overlap boundaries are already endpoint events, so there is no need to create an event for every interior point. Other members' endpoints or crossings may still occur inside. At the end boundary, members that actually end leave and others continue; both may also end together. The recorded interval is never shortened, and no boundary points are appended for the same pair. A third, shorter member does not split other pairs' complete intervals."

