msgstr "This learning flow covers ordinary crossings, empty sets and disjoint inputs, neighbor checks, distinct positions at the same sweep coordinate, endpoint contacts, multiple segments meeting at one point, zero-length points, vertical segments, collinear overlaps, and mixed events in the existing examples. Vertical segments are processed upward in y at a fixed x; collinear overlaps are represented by complete closed intervals. These preset teaching cases are not a production implementation guarantee for arbitrary degenerate inputs."

