#: src/algorithms/segment-intersection/bo/help/HelpContent.tsx:25
msgid "help.LearningReferences.5"
msgstr "Vertical cases follow the same closed-segment, lexicographic, and same-point grouping rules. The vertical status marker represents this page's processing frontier, not a unique intersection between the sweep line and the segment. Internally, a reversible exact shear (x + s·y, y) is used. Rational bounds on s are derived from the input coordinates to preserve the original lexicographic order of all endpoints and segment intersections; the display restores the original coordinates. This order-preserving derivation belongs to this implementation: the lecture is not cited as proof of the shear bound, and floating-point epsilon is not used to decide geometric relations."

